+# 007B draft acceptance coverage
+
+**Version:** 0.3 · **Prepared:** 16 November 2026, Asia/Dhaka · **Author:** JARVIS, Architect
+
+**Status: PRE-RECON PLANNING / REVIEW DRAFT. Not an implementation-ready module or execution release.**
+
+## Status and interpretation
+These 32 criteria are draft planning coverage, not frozen acceptance. “Approved/frozen policy” deliberately refers to technical mechanisms from E1 and defaults ruled by the Director. Such references must become precise observable rules before E2; unresolved placeholders cannot be graded as PASS. AC-032 is the separately released deployment boundary; it is not silently required as completed before the pre-deployment Gate Q.
+
+| ID | Area | Draft observable outcome | Decision dependencies | Required evidence level |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| AC-001 | Owner boundary | Only an authenticated owner can start/confirm an Add Store operation for that account; admin/member/unrelated-owner direct requests are denied. | D-09 | Real application/API and tenant-negative proof |
+| AC-002 | Store identity | New input validates NPI and optional NCPDP rules; simultaneous attempts for the same NPI cannot yield two stores or charge unrelated owners; duplicate NPI routes to support. | D-01 | Database-backed concurrency and UI validation |
+| AC-003 | Charge disclosure and consent | Owner sees the server-derived incremental charge, currency, billing-period effect and applicable discount before confirming; stale/tampered quotes are handled under the frozen quote policy. | D-01,D-06,D-10 | Server/UI tests plus actual sandbox invoice comparison |
+| AC-004 | Paid activation | A signed, confirmed payment event authorizes exactly one intended store activation and the correct billable quantity; browser return or forged request cannot activate it. Pending stores expose no data and grant no access. | D-01 | Signed event/live sandbox and authorization negatives |
+| AC-005 | Failed additional payment | Decline or incomplete authentication leaves the new store pending and preserves existing-store access and correct existing billing state. A pending store grants no access and exposes no data. | D-01 | Actual sandbox failure plus API/DB/UI checks |
+| AC-006 | Idempotent retry | Double submit, retry with a new key, network timeout, duplicate/out-of-order delivery and concurrent retry resolve to one intended operation, one account customer and one charge without duplicate stores. A retry with a new key and a network timeout reconcile to one operation, one customer and one payment session. No operation is closed as unpaid without proof from the provider. | D-01 | Controlled fault/concurrency tests plus owned event receipts |
+| AC-007 | Pending recovery | An interrupted payment/setup can be inspected and resumed or expired under the agreed policy, with safe NPI handling and visible operator recovery. | D-01 | Fault injection, restart and recovery evidence |
+| AC-008 | Quantity consistency | Provider quantity, local billable-store count and access reconcile across Add Store, renewal, cancellation and pending operations; no raw provider quantity change grants unnamed-store access. | D-01,D-03 | Provider/local comparisons and race tests |
+| AC-009 | Catalogue preservation | One graduated item retains $99/$49 pricing and one subscription per account; owner-only billing and existing cancellation/undo behavior remain valid. | D-06 | Catalogue identity, invoice and billing regression |
+| AC-010 | Authorized invitation | Owner/admin invitation rights follow the frozen role matrix; a store admin cannot appoint an owner/admin or act on another store. | D-02 | API/DB denial and successful intended role journey |
+| AC-011 | Invitation acceptance | A valid controlled recipient can accept and receive only the intended store/role; existing/new identities follow the approved identity policy. | D-02 | Actual email/inbox and browser proof for both identity cases |
+| AC-012 | Invitation abuse | Expired/revoked/replayed/altered invitations fail safely; link GET does not redeem, explicit button POST does. Wrong-user acceptance requires deliberate identity switching; altered account/store targets are denied. Opening the emailed link (GET) does not accept the invitation; only the explicit action (POST) does. | D-02 | Token and browser negative coverage |
+| AC-013 | Resend and revoke | Resends, duplicates and revocation obey explicit token validity, delivery and dedupe rules; old links cannot revive revoked authority. | D-02 | Delivery counters and link-state tests |
+| AC-014 | Admin replacement | Owner-controlled replacement keeps the incumbent admin until the replacement accepts and preserves exactly one effective admin per active store through acceptance, concurrency, expiration and failure. | D-02 | Database concurrency and two-identity browser journey |
+| AC-015 | Member revocation | Authorized removal ends store access at application and data layers while preserving records; test already-issued direct tokens and measure/state any residual against the frozen policy rather than silently accepting it. | D-02 | Fresh and existing-session tests plus direct API checks |
+| AC-016 | Last-admin protection | Self-removal or conflicting role changes cannot orphan an active store; the approved owner/support recovery remains possible. | D-02,D-04 | Concurrency, denial and recovery proof |
+| AC-017 | Tenant and role isolation | Owner/admin/member/unrelated-owner checks cover both apps and protected fields; invitation or handoff grants no extra billing or cross-tenant rights. | D-02 | Independent role-by-route/API/DB matrix |
+| AC-018 | Scheduled removal | Named-store removal takes effect at the approved paid-period boundary; access and quantity change coherently, records remain, and repeat jobs/events are safe. | D-03 | Controlled time/event and provider/local evidence |
+| AC-019 | Removal undo | Undo is allowed before the paid period ends; the frozen cutoff semantics are enforced before/at/after that boundary; pending add/remove/renewal changes cannot silently overcharge or reactivate a store. | D-03 | Boundary and concurrency tests |
+| AC-020 | Last-store lifecycle | Last-store removal uses whole-account cancellation and prevents an invalid zero-store subscription/access state and preserves owner billing recovery. | D-03 | Whole-account lifecycle proof |
+| AC-021 | Support transfer authority | Only the specifically authorized support operation can transfer a store after required ownership checks, with an auditable request and approved effective time. | D-04 | Authorized operator flow and denial controls |
+| AC-022 | Transfer billing and access | Buyer uses separate account/billing, seller loses access at the agreed boundary, and neither party receives the other card/subscription authority; retries are safe. | D-04 | Two-account end-to-end transition and recovery |
+| AC-023 | History and receivables | Stable store ID/records survive transfer; seller receivables follow the explicit policy. Buyer historical-claims access is denied under the approved clean-slate default; a stable ID or NPI grants no authority. | D-04 | Synthetic before/after access and data assertions |
+| AC-024 | Owner/admin recovery audit | The approved recovery process restores only verified authority, records operator/actor/reason/effect and rejects unauthorized identity substitution. | D-04 | Controlled recovery and audit proof |
+| AC-025 | O-1 live lifecycle | An isolated sandbox test clock on a multi-store account proves failed renewal, seven days normal access with banner, subsequent read-only, owner billing recovery and restored access. Cancel/undo/retry cannot reset grace; the time-control seam is unreachable in production configuration. Proved on an account with more than one store. The time-control seam is unreachable in a production configuration, shown by a negative test. | D-06,D-07 | Live test-clock/provider delivery plus application access proof |
+| AC-026 | O-2 email delivery | The reminder schedule chosen by the Director in D-05 reaches the controlled intended inbox with truthful status/links; delivery is separate from generated-link and notification-record evidence. Approved schedule: one notice at failure and one before read-only; each type at most once per failed invoice, suppressed after recovery. E1 proposes the exact pre-read-only offset for freeze. | D-05,D-07 | Provider receipt plus actual inbox observation |
+| AC-027 | Reminder reliability | Duplicate processing and send failure/retry preserve the Director-approved D-05 reminder count and dedupe policy; no reminder is sent after recovery. Validate the default-on mail guard before the first dispatch and count every attempt. The mail guard is validated before the first send; every dispatch attempt is counted. | D-05,D-07 | Controlled fault evidence, counters and inbox checks |
+| AC-028 | 007A regression | First-store purchase/provisioning, email confirm-button flow, both-direction handoff, different-user recovery, owner billing, cancellation/undo and logout remain correct. Required regression includes webhook recovery behaviours from 007A (unfinished work stays retryable; operator recovery). | D-09 | QA-controlled production-build browser and necessary live regression |
